    ['What should a mileage reimbursement form include?', 'For each trip: the date, the destination, the business purpose and the miles. IRS Publication 463 lists those as the details that prove car use. Add your name, the period the claim covers, the rate per mile, the total, your signature and the approver\'s signature.'],
    ['What mileage rate goes on a 2026 reimbursement form?', 'The IRS rate for the date of each trip: ' + c(h1.business) + ' a business mile from January 1 to June 30, 2026 and ' + c(h2.business) + ' from July 1. Medical and military moving miles are ' + c(h1.medical) + ', then ' + c(h2.medical) + '. Charity miles are 14¢ all year. Your employer can pay its own rate instead.'],
    ['My June trips are paid in August. Which rate applies?', c(h1.business) + ' a mile. Announcement 2026-11 keeps the earlier rates for allowances paid for driving before July 1, 2026, even when the payment comes later. The ' + c(h2.business) + ' rate is for driving on or after July 1, paid on or after July 1.'],
    ['How soon should I hand in my mileage form?', 'Your employer\'s policy sets the deadline. For the tax rules, IRS Publication 463 treats accounting for an expense within 60 days after it was paid or incurred as a reasonable period, and returning any excess within 120 days.'],
    ['Is mileage reimbursement taxable?', 'Not when it is paid under an accountable plan at or below the federal rate (the IRS standard mileage rate): it stays out of box 1 of your Form W-2. If the allowance is above the federal rate, the excess goes in box 1 and is taxed as wages.'],
    ['Does the IRS have an official mileage reimbursement form?', 'No. Employers use their own form. The sample mileage log in IRS Publication 463 (Table 5-2) is marked as not an official Internal Revenue form. A form like this one, with the trips, the rate, the total and the signatures, is what an employer needs to check the claim.'],
